    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=089b582f-0a35-44db-98f2-170a98083ab9&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204519102446_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Healthcare Laboratory Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\n\nLocation: Trenton\n\nHealthcare Laboratory Assistant U22: $69,373.45 - $111,006.97 (Salaries for internal candidates are determined by a promotional formula. Salaries for external candidates are determined up to step 4: $79,781.83, or dependent on qualifications) W. Cary Edwards School of Nursing and Health Professions 301 West State Street Trenton, NJ 08618 Thomas Edison State University was founded in 1972 to break down barriers to degree completion. Fifty years later, it proudly serves a diverse body of adult students with innovative and professionally relevant academic programming in a predominantly online delivery. Our team of high-energy student-focused professionals is welcoming new members who are making their mark in education and are ready to help change the lives of thousands of adult students across New Jersey and around the world. Candidates who are excited by changing lives, committed to the success of all and want to be challenged by new and innovative opportunities, should submit an application. Summary:  The W. Cary Edwards School of Nursing and Health Professions is seeking a detail-oriented Healthcare Laboratory Assistant to support the day-to-day operation of the School’s experiential learning environments. Partnering with the Director of Experiential Learning, the Assistant helps run high-fidelity simulations and skills laboratory sessions and, as the program grows, will support the School’s new virtual reality (VR) lab. Working alongside mentors and students, the Assistant maintains and organizes the laboratories, prepares materials and equipment for each session, assists during simulations and skills practice, and ensures every learning space is clean, safe, well-stocked, and ready for use. This role requires strong organization, attention to detail, and comfort with laboratory and simulation technology. Responsibilities: The Healthcare Laboratory Assistant will: - Set up and organize laboratory equipment, supplies, and materials for scheduled skills, simulation, and VR lab sessions - Clean, sanitize, and reset laboratory equipment and workspaces before and after each use, in accordance with infection-control and safety standards - Ensure all laboratory and simulation equipment is in working order; troubleshoot minor issues and report malfunctions or needed repairs to the Director of Experiential Learning - Maintain inventory of laboratory and simulation supplies and assist with ordering, receiving, and stocking as needed - Assist with the setup, operation, and breakdown of simulation scenarios, including the preparation, moulage, and positioning of high-fidelity mannequins and task trainers - Support the Director of Experiential Learning in programming, running, and resetting simulation scenarios as directed - Prepare simulated medications, charts, and supplies so scenarios run smoothly and realistically - Assist mentors during skills lab sessions by setting up practice stations and providing materials and equipment to students as needed - As the VR lab is established, assist with the setup, use, sanitizing, and safe storage of VR headsets, controllers, and related hardware and software, and help mentors and students launch VR learning modules - Maintain accurate records of laboratory usage, equipment, and inventory, and enter student data into designated databases and learning- or simulation-management systems - Assist with scheduling laboratory sessions and coordinating laboratory activities - Perform related administrative and clerical duties as assigned, including filing, data entry, and maintaining laboratory documentation Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: - Strong organizational and time-management skills, with attention to detail and the ability to follow instructions accurately - Good communication and interpersonal skills and a professional, service-oriented approach - Ability to work independently and as part of a team - Comfort learning and troubleshooting new technology, including simulation and VR equipment Proficiency with MS Office Suite, Google Workspace, and Learning Management Systems - Ability to lift and move up to 50 pounds, stand for extended periods, and perform repetitive tasks with the manual dexterity to handle laboratory, simulation, and VR equipment Requirements: Education: Graduation from an accredited college with a Bachelor's degree or equivalency as determined by the appointing authority.    Experience: Experience: Two years professional experience in a field that is directly related to the functions of the position to be filled or equivalency as determined by the appointing authority.     - Applicants who do not possess the required education may substitute required experience on a year-for-year basis (30 credit hours is considered one year of college).   - A Ph.D. degree or Ed.D. degree may be substituted for two years of the required experience.  Preferred Requirements: - Previous experience in a laboratory, simulation, or healthcare environment - Basic understanding of healthcare practices and terminology - Familiarity with simulation, audiovisual, or virtual reality technology   *TESU strives to offer a flexible work environment while balancing the operational needs of the University. As such, we have several options for hybrid-work schedules. Positions determine what type of hybrid-work schedule is available and, if necessary, adjustments are made to support University operations.    Thomas Edison State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=089b582f-0a35-44db-98f2-170a98083ab9&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204592594260_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Hourly Content Development Pre-Production Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-13\n\nLocation: Trenton\n\nHourly Content Development and Pre-Production Assistant Part-time/Hourly: $25-$30/hour, 25 hours/week Office of Communications 111 West State Street Trenton, NJ 08608   Thomas Edison State University was founded in 1972 to break down barriers to degree completion. Fifty years later, it proudly serves a diverse body of adult students with innovative and professionally relevant academic programming in a predominantly online delivery. Our team of high-energy student-focused professionals is welcoming new members who are making their mark in education and are ready to help change the lives of thousands of adult students across New Jersey and around the world. Candidates who are excited by changing lives, committed to the success of all and want to be challenged by new and innovative opportunities, should submit an application. Summary: The Hourly Content Development and Pre-Production Assistant is responsible for identifying, developing, and coordinating compelling stories that showcase the impact of Thomas Edison State University. Working collaboratively with the Director of Multimedia and the Office of Communications, this position manages the storytelling pipeline from concept through production by researching story opportunities, cultivating relationships across the University community, coordinating interviews and logistics, and providing editorial support that helps bring authentic stories to life. This position helps ensure that every student, graduate, and employee has the opportunity to share stories that demonstrate the transformative impact of a Thomas Edison State University education. The ideal candidate has a strong background in journalism, communications, or content production and possesses exceptional storytelling instincts, organizational skills, and the ability to build meaningful relationships with students, alumni, and staff. Essential Responsibilities: Story Development & Research - Research and identify compelling student, alumni, staff, and community stories that align with the University's strategic priorities. - Conduct outreach and relationship-building with prospective story participants. - Perform background research and pre-interviews to evaluate story potential. - Develop story concepts and recommend opportunities for multimedia, written, and digital content. - Build and maintain a robust pipeline of future storytelling opportunities. Editorial & Content Development - Review interviews and identify compelling soundbites and narrative themes. - Draft story summaries, interview briefs, scripts, and supporting written content. - Collaborate on the development of videos, feature stories, social media campaigns, podcasts, and other communications materials. - Help shape stories that reflect the University's mission while creating emotional connections with audiences. Production Coordination - Coordinate interview schedules, filming logistics, and production calendars. - Serve as the primary point of contact for story participants throughout the production process. - Track projects from initial outreach through final publication. - Maintain production schedules, deadlines, and project documentation. - Assist with obtaining releases, approvals, and supporting materials. Communications Collaboration - Work closely with communications staff to align storytelling efforts with institutional initiatives. - Coordinate with writers, designers, photographers, videographers, and marketing staff to maximize the impact of each story. - Help identify opportunities to repurpose stories across multiple communication platforms. Strategic Storytelling - Monitor trends, university initiatives, and community developments to proactively identify meaningful storytelling opportunities. - Recommend story ideas that support enrollment, alumni engagement, fundraising, institutional reputation, and staff communications. - Help establish consistent storytelling processes and editorial standards for the Multimedia team. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: - Outstanding storytelling and editorial judgment. - Ability to recognize meaningful stories and transform ideas into compelling content. - Strong interviewing and relationship-building skills. - Excellent written and verbal communication. - Ability to coordinate multiple projects simultaneously. - Attention to detail and commitment to quality. - Collaborative mindset with the ability to work across departments. - Strategic thinking with an understanding of audience engagement and brand storytelling. Requirements: - Bachelor's degree in Journalism, Communications, Public Relations, English, or a related field. - Professional experience in journalism, television news, communications, public relations, or content production. - Exceptional writing, interviewing, and editing skills. - Strong organizational and project management abilities. - Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. - Ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Preferred Requirements: - Experience producing editorial or broadcast / digital content. - Experience managing content calendars and production schedules. - Familiarity with multimedia storytelling and digital content strategies. - Experience collaborating with diverse stakeholders across an organization.   *TESU strives to offer a flexible work environment while balancing the operational needs of the University. As such, we have several options for hybrid-work schedules. Positions determine what type of hybrid-work schedule is available and, if necessary, adjustments are made to support University operations.  Thomas Edison State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=089b582f-0a35-44db-98f2-170a98083ab9&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204517781619_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Health Professions Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-06\n\nLocation: Trenton\n\nHealth Professions Program Coordinator  D27: $105,000 - $110,000 W. Cary Edwards School of Nursing and Health Professions 301 West State Street Trenton, NJ 08618  Thomas Edison State University was founded in 1972 to break down barriers to degree completion. Fifty years later, it proudly serves a diverse body of adult students with innovative and professionally relevant academic programming in a predominantly online delivery. Our team of high-energy student-focused professionals is welcoming new members who are making their mark in education and are ready to help change the lives of thousands of adult students across New Jersey and around the world. Candidates who are excited by changing lives, committed to the success of all and want to be challenged by new and innovative opportunities, should submit an application.   Summary:  The selected candidate of the Health Professions Program Coordinator position will be responsible for scheduling all nursing and health professions programs academic activities, both undergraduate and graduate, to meet student needs. The Health Professions Program Coordinator will be primarily responsible for overseeing and maintaining the BSNA curriculum. The Health Professions Program Coordinator will oversee course coordination, support mentors and educators, and guide students to ensure a high-quality, cohesive educational experience. While not responsible for direct teaching, the Health Professions Program Coordinator must understand online and hybrid curriculum delivery, active learning strategies, and the development of valid and reliable assessment methods.   Examples of Work:  - Coordinate the delivery of all courses within a designated program, ensuring alignment with program outcomes, accreditation standards, and evidence-based teaching practices. - Oversee the implementation of online learning experiences ensuring they are consistently aligned with program outcomes. - Participate in regular meetings with staff, mentors, and educators to review curriculum alignment, share updates, and address challenges to ensure consistency in course delivery. - Interface with third-party vendors for student resource procurement, setup, and maintenance including ATI, Wolters Kluwer Coursepoint+, and Examsoft. - Prepare third-party resources such as eBooks, interactive resources, and NCLEX-RN prep for prelicensure students. - Serve as a mentor resource, providing guidance on course policies, grading standards, and instructional methods to promote a unified approach across sections. - Participate in the planning and delivery of course orientations and educational sessions for mentors and educators, ensuring alignment with program standards and promoting consistency in instruction and assessment. - Collaborate with mentors and educators in addressing student inquiries and implementing effective teaching strategies that support a cohesive learning environment. - Facilitate the student-to-student (peer mentoring) support programs to foster student success. - Participate in the planning and delivery of student success and engagement functions such as student orientation, pinning, and commencement. - Facilitate the administration of course assessments ensuring they meet program standards and are applied consistently across courses. - Coordinate the exam blueprinting and item analysis process. - Track and review student performance data and provide feedback to ensure alignment with learning outcomes and recommend areas for improvement. - Participate in program evaluation and accreditation processes to maintain transparency, uphold high standards, and ensure regulatory compliance.   Knowledge, Skills, Abilities:  - Strong organizational and time management skills. - Attention to detail. - Good communication and interpersonal skills. - Ability to work independently and as part of a team. - Proficiency with computer applications (e.g., MS Office Suite, Google G suite, Learning Management Systems). - Experience with instructional support technologies (e.g., ATI, Publishers’ digital platforms, ExamSoft) preferred Experience in online nursing education. - Enhanced customer service knowledge. - Perform other appropriate and reasonably required duties assigned by the Dean. - This position is based in an office environment with exposure to standard skills, but mobility for travel to TESU is expected.   Requirements:  Education: A MSN degree is required. Experience: A minimum of three years’ experience preferred.   *TESU strives to offer a flexible work environment while balancing the operational needs of the University. As such, we have several options for hybrid-work schedules. Positions determine what type of hybrid-work schedule is available and, if necessary, adjustments are made to support University operations.   Thomas Edison State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=089b582f-0a35-44db-98f2-170a98083ab9&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204481881697_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Graduate Recruiting Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-03\n\nLocation: Trenton\n\nGraduate Recruiting Manager D26: $85,000 - $90,000 Division of Enrollment Management 111 W. State Street Trenton, NJ 08608 Thomas Edison State University was founded in 1972 to break down barriers to degree completion. Fifty years later, it proudly serves a diverse body of adult students with innovative and professionally relevant academic programming in a predominantly online delivery. Our team of high-energy student-focused professionals is welcoming new members who are making their mark in education and are ready to help change the lives of thousands of adult students across New Jersey and around the world. Candidates who are excited by changing lives, committed to the success of all and want to be challenged by new and innovative opportunities, should submit an application.   Summary: The Graduate Recruiting Manager works as part of the Graduate Recruitment Team in the Enrollment Management division of Thomas Edison State University. This person is part of an energetic and innovative team of university recruiting professionals that recruit individual Graduate students from various sources including Community Colleges, Four-year Colleges and Universities, Government Organizations, Corporations, non-profit organizations, and on an individual level. The Graduate Recruiting Manager develops and implements face to face recruiting outreach and virtual outreach opportunities to recruit students to the University’s Graduate academic programs. The Graduate Recruiting Manager is a critical part of the University team and cultivates and maintains strong professional relationships with personnel in all areas of the University. The Graduate Recruiting Manager is part of a team responsible for developing and implementing recruiting practices and procedures that enhance the prospect, applicant and student admissions and enrollment experience and grow enrollments. The Graduate Recruiting Manager will collaborate broadly with units from across campus and work extensively with the Enrollment Management’s admissions and marketing teams. The recruiter is expected to;  - Understand that the University has enrollment goals and that they and the Enrollment Management team are critical components of achieving the University goals. - Work collaboratively with the Enrollment Management team. - Provide innovative ideas to recruit students face to face and in a virtual environment. - Provide exceptional customer service to all students and guests and providing timely follow-up with prospective students. - Respond to prospective students and answer questions via phone, e-mail, and mail in a timely manner. - Work with the Enrollment Management team in analyzing application and enrollment trends in order to develop innovative recruitment strategies; assessing the effectiveness and adjusting strategies as necessary. - Attend recruitment events and make presentations to prospective and admitted students at various organizations and events. These events include some evening and weekend activities. - Develop and maintain knowledge and understanding of current admissions standards and degree requirements. - Manage relationships with organizations that have historically provided new students to the University. - Work with the Office of Communications to leverage social media to connect and communicate with prospective students. - Understanding FAFSA deadlines, process, procedures, and changes in order to accurately assist students.   Examples of Work: - Grow enrollments in Graduate degree programs. - Recruit Graduate students at face to face and virtual events, sometimes during nights and weekends. - Collaborate with the University Admissions office to enhance the admissions process for Graduate prospects, applicants and students. - Collaborate with University Marketing to develop and implement innovative traditional and digital marketing, targeting Graduate prospects, applicants and students. - Host webinars to engage with Graduate prospects. - Host individual appointments with prospective and returning Graduate students.   Knowledge Skills & Abilities: - Ability to recruit students to the University. - Excellent written and verbal communication skills. - Ability to develop and implement innovative recruitment ideas. - Experience in developing and conducting compelling face-to-face and virtual recruiting events. - Presenting information clearly and concisely. - Planning, organizing, and implementing workshops, programs, and conferences. - Experience speaking publicly to small and large groups. - Ability to operate independently, exercising independent judgment and discretion and with little or no guidance.   Minimum Qualifications: - Valid driver's license - Daily travel required year-round. Local and Domestic travel required. Position will require use of personal car, with mileage and tolls reimbursed according to federal guidelines. Home office. Evening and weekends as needed. - Ability to lift and move 40 pounds.   Requirements: Education: A Bachelor's degree is required. Experience in Undergraduate or Graduate recruiting can be substituted for educational qualifications as determined by the appointing authority. Experience: A minimum of two years’ experience in higher education admissions, advising and/or transfer services and/or recruiting or equivalent experience as determined by the appointing authority. Communication: Excellent communication skills and the ability to operate independently and to develop and implement innovative recruiting plans and programs at the Undergraduate and/or Graduate levels.   Preferred Requirements: - Thomas Edison State University is seeking an innovative professional with a history of success in recruiting, public relations, sales, marketing, or related fields. - The ideal candidate will have extensive recruiting experience in higher education and/or student transfer operations. - The ideal candidate will be able to quickly obtain an understanding of Thomas Edison State University undergraduate and graduate degree programs, organizational structures, academic and administrative policies and procedures.     *TESU strives to offer a flexible work environment while balancing the operational needs of the University. As such, we have several options for hybrid-work schedules. Positions determine what type of hybrid-work schedule is available and, if necessary, adjustments are made to support University operations.  Thomas Edison State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=089b582f-0a35-44db-98f2-170a98083ab9&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204517798921_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Hourly Clinical Mentor Contract Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-23\n\nLocation: Trenton\n\nHourly Clinical Mentor Contract Coordinator  Part-Time/Hourly: $25/hr 25 hrs/week W. Cary Edwards School of Nursing and Health Professions 301 West State Street Trenton, NJ 08618 Thomas Edison State University was founded in 1972 to break down barriers to degree completion. Fifty years later, it proudly serves a diverse body of adult students with innovative and professionally relevant academic programming in a predominantly online delivery. Our team of high-energy student-focused professionals is welcoming new members who are making their mark in education and are ready to help change the lives of thousands of adult students across New Jersey and around the world. Candidates who are excited by changing lives, committed to the success of all and want to be challenged by new and innovative opportunities, should submit an application.   Summary: The W. Cary Edwards School of Nursing and Health Professions is seeking a detail-oriented, part-time Clinical Mentor Contract Coordinator to manage the full contract lifecycle for the School's Clinical Mentors — independent contractors who provide clinical instruction to undergraduate nursing students at healthcare facilities throughout New Jersey. Each eight (8) week term, the Coordinator ensures that every Clinical Mentor is credentialed, contracted, and paid accurately and on time. This role is the administrative backbone of the School's clinical instruction model and requires exceptional organization, follow-through, and professional communication.   Responsibilities: The Clinical Mentor Contract Coordinator will: - Secure a current curriculum vitae (CV) or resume from each Clinical Mentor - Store Clinical Mentor credentials, contracts, and related documentation in the University's designated secure system, in compliance with University records and confidentiality policies - Collaborates with the clinical compliance coordinator to confirm that each Clinical Mentor has completed all required onboarding and compliance requirements (e.g., licensure verification, CPR certification, liability insurance, health clearances, and background check) prior to the start of each contract - Coordinate with the Assistant Director of Clinical Health Professions every term to determine Clinical Mentor course and clinical site assignments - Communicate with each Clinical Mentor every term to verify contracted dates, times, and clinical hours - Develop one (1) independent contractor agreement, with corresponding scope of work, per Clinical Mentor per term using the University's approved contract template - Secure a signed independent contractor agreement from each Clinical Mentor every term, prior to the start of services - Issue the University's independent contractor invoice form to each Clinical Mentor at the appropriate point in the contract period - Collect completed independent contractor invoices at contract end, verify them against the executed contract, and submit them for payment processing - Track contract status, outstanding documents, and payment submission for all active Clinical Mentors and report status to program leadership - Maintain professional, responsive communication with Clinical Mentors, the Clinical Coordinator, and University offices (e.g., Human Resources, Treasury) - Perform related administrative duties as assigned   Requirements: - Associate degree or higher  - Two (2) or more years of administrative, contract administration, credentialing, or program support experience - Demonstrated ability to manage recurring, deadline-driven processes with a high degree of accuracy - Strong written and verbal communication skills and a professional, service-oriented approach - Proficiency with MS Office (Word, Excel, Outlook), Adobe/e-signature tools, and web-based systems - Ability to handle confidential contractor information with discretion, consistent with University policy   Preferred Requirements: - Bachelor's degree - Experience in higher education, healthcare credentialing, or clinical placement coordination - Familiarity with independent contractor (1099) documentation and invoicing workflows *TESU strives to offer a flexible work environment while balancing the operational needs of the University. As such, we have several options for hybrid-work schedules. Positions determine what type of hybrid-work schedule is available and, if necessary, adjustments are made to support University operations.  Thomas Edison State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer",
      "department": ""
